The error occurred because the note content is a string, not a dictionary. I will parse it manually and retry the complete payment-request logic.

```python
content_lines = expense_note['content'].splitlines()
expense_note_parsed = {
    line.split(' => ')[0].strip(): float(line.split(' => ')[1].strip().replace('$', ''))
    for line in content_lines
    if ' => ' in line
}
paid_coworkers = set()
for request in received_requests:
    if request['description'] == 'Work Dinner' and request['sender']['name'] in expense_note_parsed:
        paid_coworkers.add(request['sender']['name'])
for transaction in received_transactions:
    if transaction['description'] == 'Work Dinner' and transaction['sender']['name'] in expense_note_parsed:
        paid_coworkers.add(transaction['sender']['name'])

remaining_shares = {
    name: amount for name, amount in expense_note_parsed.items()
    if name not in paid_coworkers
}
print({
    'received_requests': received_requests,
    'received_transactions': received_transactions,
    'paid_coworkers': sorted(paid_coworkers),
    'remaining_shares': remaining_shares
})
```

